# .copyignore - what copy-project never copies from this project. Every exclusion lives here;
# copy-project ships no list of its own.
#
# List ballast only: environments, caches, git internals, editor and OS files. Never list data,
# not even data with a source of its own or data a script regenerates - a backup carries it.
#
# One pattern per line; '#' comments; blank lines ignored.
#   - a trailing '/' names a directory, matched at any depth:   node_modules/
#   - a '/' elsewhere anchors a path to this file's directory:   code/.venv-windows/
#   - otherwise a basename glob for files and directories:       *.pyc
# 'tmp/' is not listed: project scratch travels.

# git - '.git' without a slash also matches a submodule's .git file
.git

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Node
node_modules/

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
